Welcome to my end-to-end data analysis project where I explore the world of used cars using Python 🐍, SQL 🗄️, Power BI 📊, and DAX ⚡.

🔍 What I Did

🧹 Data Cleaning with Pandas: handled missing values, transformed columns, and prepared features.

🗄️ SQL Queries: solved real-world business problems like:

Top companies by average selling price 💰

Market share by fuel type ⛽

Car age impact on selling price 📉

📊 Power BI Dashboards:

Multi-page navigation (Overview, Car Insights 🚗, Regional Trends 🌍)

Interactive slicers, drill-throughs, and dynamic KPIs

⚡ DAX Measures: calculated profit margins, rankings, and company-wise contributions.

📈 Key Insights

🏆 Premium brands dominate average selling price.

⛽ Diesel cars rule older models, while Petrol & EVs shine in newer ones.

🌍 Regional dashboards reveal where each brand performs best.

🎯 Why This Project?

This project reflects how a data analyst works in real life → from cleaning raw data ➡️ querying for insights ➡️ designing dashboards that drive decisions.
